index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..34f2a88f4d12e1e431173bf514b0b5e24ef303b9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-17-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/proposal.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+## Why
+
+The champion has hard-gate coverage for both installed-electric and actuator-ready ball-valve requests, but its query canonicalizer only expands abbreviated drive terms and does not preserve the material distinction between `с электроприводом` and `под электропривод`. The catalog uses the actuator-ready wording extensively, and prior Cycles 14–15 did not reach evaluation because Qdrant was unavailable; this remains a bounded, untested recall hypothesis rather than a rejected selection change.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add deterministic recognition of explicit installed-electric and actuator-ready ball-valve wording in the retrieval-query canonicalization boundary.
+- Emit at most one distinct, state-specific additive retrieval alternate using catalog-native terminology while retaining the original query and all of its constraints.
+- Require conservative phrase-level guards so negated, ambiguous, or unrelated drive wording does not create a control-state alternate.
+- Preserve hybrid fusion, candidate limits, reranker prompt/input, result text, and final-selection semantics.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion`: Produces a bounded state-specific retrieval alternate for explicit ball-valve actuation intent without asserting catalog equivalence or changing match decisions.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected product code: `src/nomenclature_matcher/query_canonicalization.py`, with existing matcher and hybrid retrieval wiring reused unchanged unless a focused compatibility adjustment is necessary.
+- Affected tests: canonicalization, hybrid retrieval, and matcher regression tests using mocks.
+- No DeepSeek prompt/model change, catalog mutation, Qdrant collection change, embedding change, or index rebuild is required.

