+## 1. State-specific canonicalization
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Extend `query_canonicalization.py` with a deterministic, phrase-allowlisted classifier for explicit installed-electric versus actuator-ready ball-valve intent; emit at most one state-specific additive alternate and preserve every source constraint. Verify focused canonicalization tests cover both states and their exact source-query preservation.
+- [ ] 1.2 Implement conservative abstention for non-ball-valve input, negation, conflicting state phrases, generic/abbreviated drive terms, and unknown wording. Verify focused negative canonicalization tests assert that no actuation alternate is emitted.
+
+## 2. Retrieval compatibility tests
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add or update mocked hybrid-retriever tests proving that a distinct state-specific alternate is queried alongside the source text, candidates remain deduplicated by LD id, and source-query candidates survive alternate retrieval failure.
+- [ ] 2.2 Add or update matcher tests proving reranking and `MatchResult.query` receive the source tender text rather than the state-specific alternate.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run the focused canonicalization, hybrid-retriever, and matcher tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; resolve implementation-test failures without changing GOLD/harness files, catalog data, prompts, or collection configuration.

